ts=2026-07-17T00:46:34.412Z type=decision scope=grepai content="grepai MCP deemed not worth using. Benchmark showed: semantic search gives poor results on this 300+ file workspace (ansible/ YAML drowns out signal for nvim config queries), can't scope queries (no --workspace), and each MCP call adds 200-400 tokens of session context overhead. Only real strength is the call graph trace feature, but that's narrow utility. Traditional grep + rtk provides better, faster results with much less context cost."
ts=2026-07-17T00:46:39.280Z type=learning scope=grepai content="grepai benchmark on nvim config (300+ file workspace): format-on-save explanation was the one win (full-file context good), but LspAttach handlers, Python LSP, autocommands all failed — grepai missed files or got drowned in ansible YAML noise. Code trace worked well for find_venv callers. Main issue: workspace not scoped (no MCP --workspace), so 300+ files diluted semantic scores. Context overhead ~200-400 tokens per query vs ~10 for grep."
